# Text is LF in every checkout, whatever core.autocrlf says. Git for Windows' installer sets it to true, and a
# plugin is installed by git clone. Git Bash reads CRLF scripts, but WSL's bash takes the CR for part of the
# interpreter's name and cannot start a hook, and checks that anchor a regex at a line end or compare bytes
# fail on CRLF. text=auto leaves binary files alone, and a file already committed with CRLF (two data tables
# and a licence) as it is.
* text=auto eol=lf
